s('Material Composition ID.', 'The MC-ID links origin, recipe, process, geometry, measurements and installed location. A component or process change creates a linked revision. A session’s assembly record identifies the exact material configuration present.', ['Provenance · source lot, supplier or custodian, permissions, assay and retained specimen.', 'Recipe · components, mass basis, particle sizes, binder and reinforcement.', 'Process · operator, equipment, cure, growth or bonding history.', 'Placement · panel address, orientation, interfaces and attachment.', 'Measurements and lifecycle · instruments, uncertainty, cleaning, repair and retirement.']),
s('A blend is also a testable assembly.', 'Clear Mind, Earthen Root, Ocean Light and Solar Code are archive blend names. Their meaningful combinations do not establish a finished recipe. Specimens compare incorporation routes, emission and particle release, moisture, cleaning and physical change.'),
s('Protected placements preserve inspection.', 'A sealed cassette, inlay or replaceable panel may be studied where a material would be unsuitable as dispersed aggregate. Conductivity, fragility, moisture response and emissions remain material-specific questions. Kintsugi seams retain their nonstructural role.'),
s('Living knowledge has custodians.', 'An ochre reference to Tasmanian Aboriginal living knowledge does not transfer knowledge rights or establish authority on Quandamooka Country. Cultural context, permissions and local relationships remain part of the provenance record.', [], ['ochre'])
